    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "This case goes to a human reviewer, and no money moves in the meantime. The reason is on the two party profiles: rider_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d is 2 (EV-RPROF-00213) and driver_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d is 2 (EV-DPROF-00213) — the same rider and this same driver, twice in the trailing 90 days, which the rider's own words ('Same driver as the last two times') confirm. Both artifacts are COMPLETE at weight 1.0, and POL-GEN-01 expressly names these two fields as citable for this test. Under POL-NS-09(c), two or more same-pair no-show disputes in 90 days is a mandatory escalation. Escalation is terminal (POL-GEN-03): no refund and no charge issues, the $6.00 cancellation fee stays on hold rather than being collected or returned, and that is where the record already has it — EV-FARE-00213 shows payment_status PENDING and refund_issued_sgd 0.00. I therefore do not reach the $4.80 driver payout the driver's side flagged as conditional (POL-NS-07), and it is neither granted nor withheld here. I also record that POL-NS-07's anti-farming check does not trip — driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 3, below the count of 4, and 3/107 completed trips is 2.8 percent, below the 8 percent rate — so nothing in that clause directs an instruction into the escalation packet, and the referrals list is empty. The lifetime counter prior_no_show_flags is not the field that clause reads and I have not used it.\n\nI could not have decided this fee on the merits in any event, and both sides should see why. The driver's GPS trace (EV-GPS-00213) is MISSING at weight 0.0 with issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT: the driver's device never uploaded, and the platform holds no trace at all for this trip. An artifact that is absent is the limiting case of impairment, so the tests that read it cannot be run. POL-NS-01 limb (b) needs the trace to place the driver inside the 150 m TRANSPORT_HUB arrival radius, and limb (c) needs the continuous dwell to be measured from the first qualifying in-geofence fix — not from the 'arrived' event. Neither can be computed. Limb (b) and limb (c) are therefore undecided: they support neither the fee the driver wants nor the failure of the clause the rider needs. On that point I accept the driver's argument, and I reject the rider's reading of POL-NS-02. The clause's 'no qualifying in-radius fix' language presupposes a trace that exists and was examined; a trace that is absent is not a trace that was searched and came up empty, and treating the two as one would convert a lost upload into an affirmative finding of non-arrival. POL-NS-02's own notes put a trace too sparse for three consecutive readings in the 'impaired, not proof of absence' column, and an absent trace sits further along that same line. So the full refund the rider asks for under POL-NS-01(b)/POL-NS-02 does not follow, and neither does the false-arrival referral she asks for under POL-NS-05(ii): that limb needs the trace to show the marker false, and with no trace we cannot say the marker was false any more than we can say it was true.\n\nWhat the working evidence does establish is the frame of the trip, not the driver's position in it. The trip record (EV-TRIP-00213, COMPLETE, weight 1.0) shows an arrived marker at 17:47:05 and the driver's termination at 17:53:40 — an interval of 395 seconds against the 300-second free waiting period in trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec — and limb (d) is satisfied on its face: no boarding event, termination by the driver, reason code RIDER_UNREACHABLE, one of the three codes the clause recognises. But the 395 seconds runs from a driver-pressed BUTTON marker (platform_policy.arrival_marker is BUTTON), and POL-NS-12 covers only a GPS_AUTO platform arrival; a button tap is exactly what POL-NS-01(c), POL-NS-05 and POL-NS-12 decline to start the clock from. The interval therefore cannot stand in for the dwell limb. The chat log (EV-CHAT-00213) is likewise MISSING at weight 0.0 with issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, yet trip_record.chat_message_count is 3, so a log did exist and was not produced; POL-NS-04 cannot be run for either party, and the loss cuts both ways — the rider cannot show an unanswered locating message and the driver cannot show that he replied. The traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-00213-01) is MISSING at weight 0.0, so POL-NS-06 limb (i) is unavailable to the driver and no accumulated dwell can be credited.\n\nThe open question the reviewer must settle is the one this record cannot answer: where the driver's vehicle actually was, and for how long, at the Jurong East MRT PHV bay between roughly 17:47 and 17:53 on 11 August 2026 — whether he was inside the 150 m TRANSPORT_HUB arrival radius and held position for the 300-second free waiting period — and, separately, what the three messages recovered by trip_record.chat_message_count actually said and when. Recovering the driver-device trace and the message export would settle both. The $6.00 remains frozen at payment_status PENDING until that review is done, and both parties keep the appeal route described in the ruling notice."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "Limb (c) does not measure dwell from the driver's recollection or from his arrival tap: the clause runs the clock from the first qualifying in-geofence GPS fix and requires a continuous dwell of at least the free waiting period in force. With no trace there is no qualifying fix, so no dwell start and no dwell length can be established, and the driver's counter-statement ('from about 5.47 to 5.53') is a party statement that cannot supply the clock the clause demands. The trip_record arrived_at of 17:47:05 is a driver-pressed BUTTON marker (trip_record.platform_policy.arrival_marker is BUTTON), and POL-NS-12 covers only a GPS_AUTO platform arrival event, so that tap cannot stand in for limb (b) or limb (c).",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-GPS-00213 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    },
    {
      "claim": "The free waiting period in force for this trip is the 300 seconds recorded in trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec, read under POL-NS-01(c), and POL-NS-06 refunds the fee in full where the effective dwell is shorter than it. The driver's own account gives him at most 5.47 to 5.53, and the record gives a marker at 17:47:05 against a cancellation at 17:53:40, but POL-NS-01(c) starts that clock from GPS entry into the geofence and not from the tap, and there is no GPS to start it. The minimum is unmet on the evidence, because nothing on this record establishes the start or the length of any qualifying in-geofence interval.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-GPS-00213 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    },
    {
      "claim": "The deciding fact — whether the driver was inside the geofence and for how long — is carried only by the gps_trace, and that artifact's weight_multiplier is 0.0. Under POL-GEN-02(2) a ruling's confidence cannot exceed the weight of the artifact that carries the deciding fact, so the cap here is 0.00 against a platform-wide floor of 0.70, and POL-NS-09(a) requires the case to go to human review. Escalation is terminal for the pipeline and holds the disputed fee rather than collecting it, so it leaves the rider not carrying the $6.00.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-GPS-00213 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    },
    {
      "claim": "Because the whole trace is absent there is no rider_track either, so POL-NS-04 limb (c) cannot be run at all. POL-NS-11 governs that situation: limb (c) is UNDECIDABLE, neither satisfied nor failed, POL-NS-04 cannot exonerate the rider, and the dispute falls to be decided on the driver's own evidence, without the absent rider track impairing the driver's arrival or dwell finding and without any inference that the rider was elsewhere.",
      "side": "DRIVER",
